Subject: d3d11: route Texture2D pixel SRVs and retain bound views

The standalone host has no WineD3D view to sample owned On12 textures.
Route the base Texture2D SRV lifecycle and pixel-stage bindings to the core,
retain textures/views with backend child references, and implement D3D11
output/input hazard unbinding. This permits byte-exact shader sampling of
initial uploads while preserving the ordinary WineD3D path. Resolve the
new exports as one required group so an older core cannot publish a partial
backend. Later-version and other resource/stage views remain unsupported.

